{"text": "MOUNTAIN VIEW\n\nREGIONAL MEDICAL CENTER\n\nMay 8, 2018\nTo the Las Cruces Community,\n\n| am writing to inform you that, after much thought and prayer, | accepted a position as the System CEO for\nNorthwest Health located in Bentonville Arkansas. With a combined active medical staff of more than 540\nphysicians, 2,200 employees and 487 beds, Northwest Health is one of the largest health networks in Northwest\n\u2018Arkansas with five hospitals. Northwest presents an environment for me to advance those principles and\nprograms that have proven so successful for us at MountainView. The opportunity to undertake the senior\nleadership role for this CHS enterprise was simply too inviting for myself and my family to pass on.\n\nWhat a joy and blessing it has been for me and my family to be part of this organization and community for the\npast ten years. In looking back it\u2019s hard to capture all the changes we, working together, accomplished.\nTogether we created an outstanding integrated health care delivery system, developed the remarkable\nMountainview Medical Group, built New Mexico's first free standing Emergency Center, launched our the first\n\u2018Trauma program for our community, expanded our hospital, created and acquired new points of entry and\n\nso much more. | will miss MountainView.\n\nEven great teams, however, can benefit from renewal of leadership from time to time. | am proud of what we\naccomplished and the path we traveled together. | am confident in the leadership team in place and the ability\nfor this change to position MountainView to do even greater things.\n\nThe process of transition has already begun. | stand committed to supporting the transition and serving as a\ncontinuing resource for MountainView into the future. We will provide you with further information as\ntimelines and actions become established.\n\n{As parents of seven children, our family is accordingly fully engaged in the public schools and local activities. |\nhave been fortunate to serve as Chair of the LCPS Foundation Board these past two years and encourage each of\nyou to continue the strong support Las Cruces demonstrates for our schools and teachers and administrators.\n\n\u2018This past year | was honored to be asked to serve as the Chair of the Greater Las Cruces Chamber Board. | regret\nthat | will not be able to complete my time in that position, but leave with full knowledge of the strength,\nstability and progress the chamber demonstrates on a daily basis.\n\nLas Cruces is a special place and our family will greatly miss being here. | offer my sincere thanks to each of you\nthat do so much, each day, to make our community stronger.\n\nSincerely,\n\nfat, lol\n\nDeitten Park\n\nAve. + Las Cruces, NM S801 +",
